  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> be a real number for which the system of linear equations</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>has infinitely many solutions. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> is a root of the quadratic equation:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
